Differnt clusters you have worked on?

In my project, I mainly worked with two types of Databricks clusters: Job Clusters and All-Purpose Clusters.

Job Clusters were used for our production ETL pipelines. These clusters are created when a job starts and automatically terminate after the job completes, which helps reduce costs and provides an isolated execution environment.

All-Purpose Clusters were used during development for writing notebooks, debugging, testing transformations, and ad-hoc data analysis. We enabled auto-termination so that idle clusters didn't incur unnecessary costs.

From a hardware perspective, we selected different VM sizes based on the workload. For regular ETL jobs, we used general-purpose clusters. For larger datasets or memory-intensive operations, we used memory-optimized nodes. If a workload was CPU-intensive, we could choose compute-optimized nodes.

I also worked with cluster configurations such as autoscaling, which automatically adjusts the number of worker nodes based on workload, Photon acceleration to improve Spark SQL and DataFrame performance, and selecting the appropriate Databricks Runtime version for compatibility and performance."

