Shuffle & Stages: "A shuffle redistributes data across partitions, and every shuffle creates a new Spark stage. In other words, shuffle boundaries determine stage boundaries."

A shuffle is the process of redistributing data across partitions and is triggered by wide transformations like join, groupBy, and repartition. A stage is a set of tasks that can execute without a shuffle.
Spark's DAG Scheduler groups all narrow transformations (such as map, filter, and select) into the same stage because they don't require data movement.
Shuffle boundaries determine stage boundaries, meaning whenever a shuffle occurs, Spark ends the current stage and starts a new one.
The relationship is that shuffle boundaries determine stage boundaries. Whenever Spark encounters a shuffle operation, it completes the current stage and creates a new stage for the operations after the shuffle.

